 "poem": "XIII. OMNES DE ILLUMINUS domine.\n145    Now come, and now go; for th' hour,\nThat thou hast all the hours of heaven,\nIs come again: thou liv'st long still again,\nAnd yet uncomplac'd art thou alone.\nIn that last, like a distant planet\nOf thy last, or sunset's spirit-bloomed zone,\nThou hast spent the night, but not the hour;\nOr though it seeme to thee so early,\nIt may be to thee but late sometime.\n[Enter BERNARD.] He will bethink somebody.\nHe sees me, and I know he does even.",
